==================================================

Use typed AG-002 errors.

Handle:

- record not found
- duplicate record
- invalid query
- invalid pagination
- version conflict
- unsupported operation
- serialization failure
- storage failure
- invalid record

Clearly classify retryable vs non-retryable errors.

Do not leak sensitive data in errors.

==================================================
14. SECURITY
==================================================

Storage abstraction must NOT bypass the security layer.

Important distinction:

Repository:
    stores/retrieves data

AuthorizationService:
    decides whether actor may access data

Service layer:
    enforces authorization before exposing data

Do not move authorization responsibility into the repository
unless an existing contract explicitly requires it.

Storage errors/logs must not expose:

- apiKey
- password
- token
- secret
- credential
- pwd
- passphrase

==================================================
15. OBSERVABILITY
==================================================

Add safe repository/storage metrics where useful:

- operation
- success/failure
- duration
- count
- page size
- conflict count

Never log raw memory content.

Never log sensitive metadata.

